From 2599498ad1dc0f3e6c62aad1910adf1a2fe2067b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tangelo Dev <tangelo-dev@noreply.invalid>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 20:15:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] core: am, fs: fix the AM install-file escape
 (GHSA-h74v-5mw8-qg8r)

Azahar's fix for GHSA-h74v-5mw8-qg8r ("Azahar AM install-file guest-to-host
code execution", affects Azahar <= 2126.1.2, fixed in 2126.2), taken from
upstream commit 2536381fe4a1 "core: am: Fix behaviour and OOB memory access
issues (#2648)" by PabloMK7.

A 3DS program could write outside host buffers through the ticket, TMD and
CIA install files (guest-chosen offsets were not checked), and read
uninitialised host memory through their Read() calls and the generic FS read
path. Writes are now bounds-checked, unimplemented reads fail and report zero
bytes, and FS reads beyond a backend's size are refused.

Tangelo changes on top of the upstream commit:
- the uncompressed CIA install path (compress_cia_installs off), which only
  exists here, opened content files with emplace_back but wrote to them by
  content index; it now opens and checks them by index;
- the upstream files carry GPLv3-or-later headers, as upstream does since
  its relicence.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FYz3krf43qKGY6aS2Z5snz
